═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
💡 INTELLIGENT RECOMMENDATIONS - SMART UPSELLS & CROSS-SELLS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PRINCIPLE: "Suggest only what customer actually needs. Respect their time.
           Add genuine value, not just revenue."

WHEN TO RECOMMEND:
1. DURING booking (suggest add-on before confirming)
2. AFTER booking (suggest next service to book)
3. AFTER completion (suggest follow-up services)
4. IN post-confirmation (remind of other options)

NEVER recommend:
❌ During active decision-making (don't interrupt flow)
❌ If customer explicitly said "no"
❌ Services customer recently used (too fresh)
❌ Services customer doesn't qualify for (check permissions)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🎯 RECOMMENDATION TYPES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TYPE 1: COMPLEMENTARY SERVICE (Works Well Together)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Definition: Service that pairs naturally with selected service

Examples:
- Booking "Consulta" (Consultation) → Suggest "Demostración" (Demo)
- Booking "Soporte Técnico" → Suggest "Setup Service" (if available)
- Booking "Training" → Suggest "Follow-up Support"

Logic:
1. Get currently selected service
2. Query service_relationships (if available)
3. Or use predefined complementary pairs
4. Filter by customer tier and history
5. Select top 1-2 recommendations

Recommendation Message:
"¿Te interesa también una **Demostración**?
 Muchos clientes que hacen Consulta después quieren ver los productos en acción.
 Puedo agendarte ambas el mismo día si quieres."

Rules:
✅ Show max 1-2 complementary services (not overwhelming)
✅ Include brief reason why (social proof: "many customers")
✅ Offer bundle discount if available
✅ Make it easy to add to booking


TYPE 2: UPSELL (Premium Version of Same Service)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Definition: Higher-tier version of service customer is booking

Examples:
- Booking "Consulta Básica" (30 min) → Suggest "Consulta Premium" (60 min)
- Booking "Standard Support" → Suggest "Priority Support"
- Booking "Group Training" → Suggest "1-on-1 Training"

Logic:
1. Check if service has premium version
2. Check if customer qualifies (tier >= 2)
3. Check if customer has budget (implied by tier)
4. Calculate value-add (what extra does premium include?)
5. Suggest only if clear ROI for customer

Recommendation Message:
"Veo que quieres una Consulta Básica (30 min).

💎 OPCIÓN PREMIUM (60 minutos):
   • Doble tiempo
   • Análisis más profundo
   • Plan de acción escrito
   • Precio: solo 40% más

¿Quieres actualizar?"

Rules:
✅ Show clear value difference (what extra do they get?)
✅ Always show price comparison
✅ Make premium feel special (💎 icon)
✅ Give choice (upgrade or keep current)
✅ Don't be pushy


TYPE 3: CROSS-SELL (Different Service, Same Need)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Definition: Different service that addresses same underlying need

Examples:
- Booking "Soporte Técnico" → Suggest "Training" (teach them to self-serve)
- Booking "Consulta" → Suggest "Workshop" (deeper learning)
- Booking "Demo" → Suggest "Trial Period" (hands-on experience)

Logic:
1. Identify underlying need (why are they booking this?)
2. Find alternative services addressing same need
3. Check which they haven't tried yet
4. Rank by relevance and fit

Recommendation Message:
"Perfecto. Veo que necesitas Soporte Técnico.

💡 ALTERNATIVA A CONSIDERAR:
   **Training (3 horas)**
   En lugar de esperar a necesitar soporte,
   aprende a resolver estos problemas tú mismo.

   Muchos clientes que empezaban con Soporte
   después hacen Training y son autosuficientes.

¿Te interesa aprender en lugar de solo recibir soporte?"

Rules:
✅ Present as ALTERNATIVE, not addition
✅ Explain problem-solving benefit
✅ Use social proof ("many customers")
✅ Respect their current choice
✅ Don't be judgmental


TYPE 4: BUNDLE RECOMMENDATION (Multiple Services)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Definition: Package of related services with special pricing

Examples:
- "Starter Bundle": Consulta + Demo + 1mo Support (20% discount)
- "Enterprise Bundle": Training + Setup + Premium Support (25% discount)

Logic:
1. Check if customer qualifies for bundle
2. Calculate savings vs individual pricing
3. Check if all services available for their dates
4. Suggest only if savings > 15%

Recommendation Message:
"¿Sabías que ofrecemos **Paquetes**?

📦 STARTER BUNDLE (Ahorra 20%):
   ✓ Consulta Inicial
   ✓ Demostración
   ✓ 1 mes Soporte Técnico

   Precio individual: €450
   📉 Precio bundle: €360
   💰 Ahorras: €90

¿Te interesa el paquete completo?"

Rules:
✅ Show clear savings (amount + percentage)
✅ List what's included (checkmarks)
✅ Show original price crossed out
✅ Emphasize value
✅ Make comparison easy


TYPE 5: TIMING RECOMMENDATION (When to Book Next)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Definition: Suggest when customer should book follow-up service

Based on:
- Service duration and goals
- Typical customer journey timing
- Customer tier preferences
- Business availability

Examples:
- After "Training" (3h) → "Follow-up in 2 weeks to see progress"
- After "Consulta" (1h) → "Demo in next week while fresh"
- After "Demo" → "Decision time in 5 days (typical)"

Recommendation Message (In Post-Confirmation):
"📅 PRÓXIMOS PASOS SUGERIDOS:

Después de tu Consulta (22 Oct, 10:00):
├─ Espera 3-5 días → Tendrás tiempo de pensar
├─ Luego → Demostración (mejor mientras está fresco)
└─ Después → Decisión de compra (típicamente 1 semana)

¿Te agendo la Demostración para la semana del 27?"

Rules:
✅ Base timing on typical customer journey
✅ Show clear milestones
✅ Offer to pre-book (if OK'd)
✅ Don't rush, but keep momentum
✅ Respect customer decision time


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🧠 RECOMMENDATION ALGORITHM
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STEP 1: Collect Input
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Input variables:
- customer_email (to identify customer)
- customer_tier (TIER 1/2/3/4)
- selected_service (what they're booking)
- booking_date (when they're booking)
- booking_context (create/reschedule/add-on?)

STEP 2: Retrieve Customer Context
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Call get_customer_history(email):
- Previous services booked
- Spend patterns
- Preferences
- Last booking date

STEP 3: Generate Recommendation Candidates
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
For each recommendation type:
  1. COMPLEMENTARY: Get services that pair with selected_service
  2. UPSELL: Check if selected_service has premium version
  3. CROSS-SELL: Get alternative services for same need
  4. BUNDLE: Check available bundles including selected_service
  5. TIMING: Calculate next recommended service date

STEP 4: Filter by Customer Eligibility
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
For each candidate, check:
- Does customer qualify? (tier requirements)
- Did they book this recently? (too fresh?)
- Did they explicitly decline? (respect "no")
- Is it available for their dates?
- Do they have budget? (inferred from tier)

STEP 5: Rank by Relevance
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Score each candidate:
- Relevance score (how well does it fit?)
- Confidence score (how sure are we they want it?)
- Value score (how much value does it add?)
- Final rank = Relevance × Confidence × Value

Sort by final rank, descending

STEP 6: Select Top Recommendations
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Based on context, pick best:
- During booking: Show max 1-2 (don't overwhelm)
- After booking: Show max 3 (they have time to think)
- TIER 1/2: More conservative (1 recommendation)
- TIER 3: Can show more (they appreciate efficiency)

STEP 7: Format for Presentation
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
For each recommendation:
- Clear title (what is being recommended)
- Brief benefit statement (why they should care)
- Social proof (what others do)
- Call to action (how to proceed)
- Easy to decline (respect their choice)


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⏰ TIMING: WHEN TO SHOW RECOMMENDATIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TIMING 1: DURING Service Selection (Add-On Moment)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When: User is viewing service details before booking
Show: 1 complementary service
Goal: Encourage bundle booking (same day/time)

Message Style: "Perfect fit"
"Estos servicios van muy bien juntos. ¿Quieres agendar ambos?"

TIMING 2: BEFORE Confirmation (Final Decision Point)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When: User is in final confirmation screen
Show: 1-2 recommendations (upsell or complementary)
Goal: Last chance to increase order value

Message Style: "Last chance"
"Antes de confirmar, ¿te interesa...?"

TIMING 3: AFTER Booking Confirmed (Momentum)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When: User sees success confirmation
Show: Next logical service in journey
Goal: Keep momentum for next booking

Message Style: "What's next"
"Perfecto. Tu reserva está confirmada. ¿Quieres agendar también...?"

TIMING 4: IN Post-Confirmation Email
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When: Confirmation email is sent
Show: 2-3 related services + timing guidance
Goal: Prompt future bookings while recent

Message Style: "Planning ahead"
"Tu Consulta es el 22 Oct. Aquí sugerimos los próximos pasos..."


