═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🚫 ANTI-PATTERNS (What NOT to do)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

❌ DON'T recommend services:
- Customer just booked (let them complete transaction first)
- Customer explicitly declined (respect "no thanks")
- Customer can't afford (check tier/history)
- Customer doesn't need (not their use case)
- Too similar to what they already book
- In overwhelming numbers (max 2 during booking)

❌ DON'T use language:
- "You probably need..." (presumptuous)
- "Upgrade now!" (too salesy)
- "Don't miss out!" (FOMO tactics)
- "Only for limited time" (artificial urgency)
- "Everyone is doing it" (fake social proof)

❌ DON'T timing:
- During active booking (interrupts flow)
- Too frequently (annoying)
- When customer is frustrated (tone-deaf)
- Before they've completed first booking (low confidence)

✅ DO recommend when:
- Service clearly adds value
- Customer is receptive (right context)
- Recommendation is relevant (checked history)
- Timing is natural (after purchase, not during)
- You have confidence it fits their needs


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
📊 A/B TESTING FRAMEWORK
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Test different recommendation strategies:

Test 1: Recommendation Placement
├─ Control: No recommendation shown
├─ Variant A: Shown before confirmation
├─ Variant B: Shown after confirmation
└─ Metric: Add-on booking rate

Test 2: Recommendation Type
├─ Control: Complementary service (safe)
├─ Variant A: Upsell (premium version)
├─ Variant B: Bundle (package deal)
└─ Metric: Average order value

Test 3: Message Style
├─ Control: "Many customers also book..."
├─ Variant A: "This would save you €50..."
├─ Variant B: "Perfect next step is..."
└─ Metric: Click-through rate

Test 4: Offer Incentive
├─ Control: No discount
├─ Variant A: 10% discount for add-on
├─ Variant B: Free add-on setup
└─ Metric: Acceptance rate


